  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-15, after he read the screenshots of PR #1717:\n\n> The issue of moving WCS setup allowing for picking, axises and origin on setup page, moving it to the WCS pane instead.. is that in there? cuz screenshots i look at does not have that functionality moved\n\nWhat happens: PR #1717 (issue #1648) moves only the Work offset (G54-G59) control to the WCS page. The group \"Set WCS from features\" stays on the Setup page. That group holds the picks that set the WCS origin and the WCS axes. The decision file `docs/decisions/1648-wcs-page-work-offset.md` kept it there.\n\nExpected: the WCS page holds all controls that set the WCS: the feature picks with their roles (Origin, X, Y, Z), the origin, the axes and the work offset. The Setup page keeps only the controls that set the part orientation on the machine.\n\nNotes:\n- The controls keep their commands. Undo and redo do not change.\n- \"Pick for WCS\" must take viewport picks from the WCS page as it does now from the Setup page (#1562).\n- Stack the branch on PR #1717, because the two change the same pages.\n- Update the structural UI tests. Do not change snapshot PNGs.\n- The PR body shows the Setup page and the WCS page, before and after.\n\nDone means: the WCS page shows the feature picks for origin and axes, the Setup page does not, a pick from the WCS page sets the WCS, and structural tests pin the two pages.\n",
